oors  but there's also sort of no  standard for developing standards and in  the united states the development of  standards is overseen by  an organization called ansi  american national standards institute  everybody calls it ansi  the lack of a federal standard the lack  of a uniform way of going about getting  a standard has created this sort of  vacuum and in that vacuum you know  people see an opportunity to come in and  and serve as experts  [Music]  uh the ceramic tile industry in the  united states put forth a standard with  ansi  at present peter irmish's walkway  management group offers the only tests  to certify people to that industry  standard and so the criticism is that  really they are testing to industry  standard not necessarily to the standard  that would prevent the most amount of  injuries  if you go down the list of laminate  floors luxury vinyl floors  all types of hard surface floors wood  floors  all hard surface floors today really  have no standards even though we've been  publishing ours for decades they will  not voluntarily adopt them in fact the  only  industry that does have a standard is  the ceramic tile industry the tile  council of north america it's a trade  association the tcna is corporate  america on steroids i mean it's the  largest manufacturers in the world who  manufacture ceramic tile who banded  together to create a trade association  who now writes standards for themselves  so it's not my standard or our standard  they adopted the standard that's used in  europe it's the european union standard  recognized by 27 countries  so it's not my standard our role in that  was that we were aware of the research  in europe and we introduced  the tile council leadership to that  research  it's called ansi a326.3  and it defines the test methodology to  determine whether a floor is slippery  and it also  gave us a threshold so you take a  digital numerical measurement  and you can either pass or fail i can  tell you since this met